course: dictionary
lesson: 9363
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word sponge can be a thing for washing, a sea animal, a cake, or even a verb meaning to wipe something clean. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context.
explain: «Forces do not only change speed: squeeze a sponge and you change its shape.» Here a sponge is a soft thing you can squeeze. «In 2021 scientists found sponges living on a rock underneath» means the sponges are sea animals, because they live on rock and not in a kitchen.
explain: Some sponge words are not about sponges at all. «Soak up like a sponge» means to learn quickly, and to sponge off someone means to keep taking money or food from them without giving back. Ask yourself: does this make sense with the meaning I chose? If not, try another.
fact: A sponge is a soft thing full of holes that soaks up water.
fact: A sea sponge is a simple animal that lives fixed to rocks, not a plant.
fact: A sponge cake is a light, soft cake, such as a Victoria sponge.
fact: To sponge something means to wipe or clean it with a wet sponge.
fact: «Sponge off» someone is informal and means taking money or food from them without giving back.
exercise: «Squeeze a sponge and you change its shape.» What kind of thing is a sponge in this sentence? | A light, soft cake | *A soft object full of holes | A sea animal | A type of rock
exercise: «In 2021 scientists found sponges living on a rock underneath.» What are these sponges? | Light, soft cakes | Holes in the ice | Soft things for washing dishes | *Sea animals that live fixed to rocks
exercise: Ella learns French words «like a sponge». What does this mean? | She soaks up water from the floor | She keeps asking her friends for money | She eats a sponge cake | *She learns them quickly
test: Dad says, «Please sponge the table.» What does he want you to do? | Pour water on it | Eat something off it | *Wipe it clean with a wet sponge | Soak it in the bath
test: Sam says, «Stop sponging off your brother!» What does sponging off mean? | Washing your brother's clothes | *Taking money or food without giving back | Sleeping in the same bed as him | Drawing pictures of him
exam: «Wetlands soak up flood water like a sponge, clean the water, and are home to many birds.» What does sponge mean in this sentence? | Money taken from someone | A light, soft cake | A sea animal living on rocks | *Something that soaks up water
